.TH write 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
write \- send a message to another logged-in user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B write
.I user
[\fIttyname\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B write
copies what you type to the terminal of
.IR user ,
who sees it prefixed with your name and terminal.  End with the
end-of-file key.
.PP
If the user is logged in more than once, give the
.I ttyname
to choose which.
.SH NOTES
The recipient must have messages enabled; see
.BR mesg (1).
Writing to a user who is not logged in, or who has messages off, gives
a message and nothing is sent.
.PP
On a machine with one screen and one keyboard this is mostly useful for
writing to another console \- the PC3 has several \- or across the
serial line.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mesg (1),
.BR wall (1),
.BR who (1)
